{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Creating a Gantt Chart: Step 1"}, {"type": "position", "content": 8}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to describe the steps of a Gantt chart. "}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe common activities at work by using short sentences in familiar spoken and written situations.  Interpret the requirements report to determine the technological needs in managing information, based on rules and protocols established by the company."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Participates in simple conversations or simulated situations about the communicative topics for this level through grammar and vocabulary structures."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Recognizes simple ideas on requirement reports, tools for Object Oriented Programming, and other basic programming tools."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob08re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Read more information about Gantt charts."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Imagine that you have your own company and you need to establish some tasks to accomplish a project."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Follow the first step to fill in a Gantt chart."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your work with your partners and instructor."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I read more about the topic."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I describe the purpose of the project for my company."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I list the tasks and fill in a Gantt chart to develop the tasks."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I explain my Gantt chart to my partners and instructor.  "}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "workaround "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a strategy to solve a problem, especially with computer and systems"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: A Gantt chart can help you set some workarounds for problems that may come out."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob08aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "come out "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "in this context, to appear"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(phrasal verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: A Gantt chart may help you to set some workarounds for problems that may come out."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob08aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "delay "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to be late or deliver something late"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If you forget any important task, the chart is not going to work, and you will delay the delivery of your project."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob08aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "keep something in mind "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "not to forget something important"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Keep the information above in mind and then start with the first step to creating a Gantt chart."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob08aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": " knock-on effect "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a side effect"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Make sure you write down all the tasks you need to execute in order to fulfill your goals and to avoid any knock-on effects."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob08aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Infinitives of Purpose - Verbs with Infinitives"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "We can use infinitives of purpose and verbs with infinitives to express why we do some things, in this case, in a process."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p>Remember that we use <strong>infinitives of purpose</strong> to express why we do something. Therefore, when talking about setting projects, we can use the <strong>infinitive of purpose</strong> to show a process and to say why we do that process.</p> <p>Examples:</p> <ul> <li><i>I create a Gantt chart to organize the tasks of the project.</i></li> <li><i>To know who is in charge of each task, the bars on the graphic have different colors.</i></li> </ul> <p>As you can see in the previous examples, if you use the <strong>infinitive of purpose</strong> clause at the beginning, you use a comma to separate the other clause. Bearing that on mind, these are the structures you follow.</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">Main clause + <strong>to</strong> + <strong>infinitive form of the verb</strong> + complement</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">Or</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>To</strong> + <strong>infinitive form of the verb</strong> + complement + , + main clause</p> <p>You can use the <strong>infinitive of purpose</strong> more politely by using the expressions <strong>in order to</strong> or <strong>so as to</strong>.</p> <p>Examples:</p> <i>I create my chart<strong> in order to</strong> have every task in order.</i></br><i>I add color on each lane of the graphic <strong>so as to</strong> show the different elements on it.</i>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Gantt charts are great tools to organize information and set up projects."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You can use the Gantt chart to organize relevant information for your project."}, {"type": "example", "content": "We can use a work breakdown structure to classify all the tasks."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Types of Charts: Distribution Charts"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p>We use <strong>distribution charts</strong> to show several types of data organization and distribution.</p>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p>We can use <strong>distribution charts</strong> to group information. These charts answer to the question: What&rsquo;s the distribution of our data? When your data shows a diversity of variables, you can use a column or line histogram, a scatter plot chart or even a cloud to distribute your data in a more qualitative way.</p>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Bar Histogram</strong></p>"}, {"type": "image", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob08img01.jpg"}, {"type": "image", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob08img02.jpg"}, {"type": "image", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob08img03.jpg"}], "type": "learning_points"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "id": 0, "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n3le01ob08re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe8n3le01ob08re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<p>Today we're going to learn how to create a Gantt Chart</p>\n<p>Gantt charts are great tools to organize information and set up projects. A Gantt chart can help you set some workarounds for problems that may come out. You can use the Gantt chart to organize relevant information for your project. For example, it can help you to designate who will be responsible for each task, how long each task is going to take, and a suitable overall time for the project.</p>\n<p>Let's see how to create a Gantt chart:</p>"}, {"time": "38000", "image": "enpe8n3le01ob08re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<p>To design a good Gantt chart, you need to think about essential activities for the success of your project; if you forget any important task, the chart is not going to work, and you will delay the delivery of your project. Consider all the tasks you have to perform, then think about the people involved in each task, and finally, calculate the time each task will take and consider any problem you should encounter during the development of the project.</p>\n<p>Keep the information above in mind and then start with the first step to creating a Gantt chart.</p>"}, {"time": "75000", "image": "enpe8n3le01ob08re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<p>First step:</p>\n<p>To start, on the left side of a piece of paper, we're going to write down all the activities we need to perform; we can use a work breakdown structure to classify all the tasks. This structure consists of dividing your project into small pieces (tasks) and arranging them into a specific order. After you assemble the tasks, you are going to write the starting date and the estimated duration next to each of them; try to locate your tasks in a suitable overall timescale.</p>\n<p>Make sure you write down all the tasks you need to execute in order to fulfill your goals and to avoid any knock-on effects.</p>"}], "coverimg": "enpe8n3le01ob08re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can explain how to create a Gantt chart by following the first step."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can describe the information that needs to be included in a Gantt chart."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about essential tasks in a Gantt chart."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "How do you schedule your projects' processes?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Do you use any graphic help to represent that schedule? Why?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type"